      <name>Mackay's Lemon Curd</name>
      <category>Other</category>
      <info>A lemon curd with 5.7g fat, carbohydrates 75g, sugars 69g, protein 1.4g, salt 0.06g per 100g
Ingredients: Sucrose, whole eggs (pasteurized), butter, modified corn starch, lemon juice. gelling agent: pectin. acidity regulator: citric acid and lemon oil
Confidence: high
Ingredient list shows sucrose as main sugar, with eggs and butter providing fat and protein. Carbohydrates mostly from sucrose, with some starch from modified corn starch. Sugars nearly all sucrose, with minor glucose/fructose from lemon juice. Butter provides most saturated fat and butterfat. MSNF and lactose are low due to small butter content. Ash, minerals, and fiber are low. Salt and sodium calculated from label. No cocoa, alcohol, or sugar alcohols. Added sugars nearly all from sucrose. Starch from modified corn starch. Values cross-checked with typical commercial lemon curd.</info>
